Basics:
=======

x -> y, given x we are predicting y or is y.

FEATURE: The input variable x above 

LABEL: The thing we are predicting, the y above

EXAMPLE: Instances with Feature
  LABELLED   : Has both labelled features, used for training
  UNLABELLED : Only features no labels

MODEL: Defines the relationship between Features and Labels (like of it as the attributes of Edges in a Graph)

TRAINING: Show the Model labelled examples and learn the relationships between Features and Labels

INFERENCE: Applying Trained Models to unlabeled examples

Models can be
 [1] Regressions: Provides continous values

 [2] Classifications: Provides discrete values





